{"id": 52, "ts": 1783954164.302501, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I remain convinced that **Candidate\u202fA** is the strongest fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role. While we still lack concrete examples of his stress\u2011resilience, the evidence we do have is compelling: A \u201ccan make correct decisions quickly,\u201d which directly satisfies our decision\u2011quality requirement under pressure, and the notes confirm he has *excellent attention skills*, supporting the critical attention\u2011to\u2011detail criterion. Moreover, I can now add that Candidate\u202fA is known to be **100\u202f% reliable**, reinforcing his operational reliability\u2014a non\u2011negotiable safety factor. His ability to create a positive atmosphere with the crew offsets the concern about his egocentric perception, and his willingness to put others\u2019 concerns first suggests sufficient crew cooperation. Although his communication and adaptability are weaker, these can be mitigated through targeted training, whereas the other candidates either lack documented reliability (C, D) or have unverified but potentially serious crew\u2011trust issues (B\u2019s nasty remarks, D\u2019s arrogance). Therefore, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fA."}
