{"id": 57, "ts": 1783954232.4617226, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I concur with Agent\u202f1\u2019s assessment and will move my provisional vote to **Candidate\u202fA**. The decisive factor for me is the concrete evidence of operational reliability (\u201c100\u202f% reliable\u201d) and excellent attention skills, both of which are non\u2011negotiable for long\u2011haul flights. In addition, A \u201ccan make correct decisions quickly\u201d and \u201ckeeps calm in a crisis,\u201d directly satisfying decision\u2011quality and stress\u2011resilience criteria. While A does have communication challenges (difficulty communicating ideas, perceived egocentricity), the notes also highlight that he creates a positive crew atmosphere and puts others\u2019 concerns above everything, suggesting that his teamwork orientation can offset those weaknesses and be reinforced through training. By contrast, Candidate\u202fB\u2019s reliability is inferred from conscientiousness but his \u201cnasty remarks\u201d and \u201cpretentious\u201d tone lack concrete impact evidence, and his weak numeric memory raises attention concerns. Candidate\u202fC, despite strong technical insight, has no documented reliability or attention evidence, and Candidate\u202fD\u2019s know\u2011it\u2011all attitude and hot temper pose clear crew\u2011cooperation risks. Therefore, A\u2019s documented reliability, attention, decision\u2011making and stress handling make him the strongest overall fit."}
